## A playing card -- in the outline style:  its name, then what's true of it
// The card says what its suits, ranks and colors are:  a deck, a pile or a game only reads them.
// A drawable thing:  each card is its own element on the page, e.g. `<cards-card>`.
a "card" is a drawable thing where:

	## suits, ranks and colors:  the card's own kinds of values
	- "suits" as one of clubs, diamonds, hearts or spades
	- "ranks" as one of ace, 2 ... 10, jack, queen or king
	- "colors" as one of red or black

	- the "color" of a suit is:
		red if it is diamonds or hearts
		black otherwise
	- the "symbol" of a suit is:
		"♣️" if it is clubs
		"♦️" if it is diamonds
		"♥️" if it is hearts
		"♠️" if it is spades
		"?" otherwise
	- a rank "is a face card" if it is jack, queen or king

	## its suit and rank
	- its "suit" is a suit
	- its "rank" is a rank
	- its "color" is the color of its suit
	- its "value" is the position of its rank      // ace 1 ... king 13

	- it "is a (suit)"                              // e.g. "the card is a spade"
	- it "is a (rank)"                              // e.g. "the card is a queen"
	- it "is the (rank) of (suits)"                 // e.g. "the card is the queen of spades"
	- it "is a face card" if its rank is a face card
	- it "is the (color as a color) joker" if it is a joker and its color is color

	## its direction:  face up or face down
	- its "direction" is up or down
	- it "is face up" if its direction is up
	- it "is face down" if its direction is down

	## its names
	- its "name" is: its rank + "-of-" + its suit   // e.g. "queen-of-spades"
	- its "short suit" is the symbol of its suit
	- its "short rank" is:
		"?" if its rank is nothing
		"" + its rank if its rank is a number
		the first character of its rank as uppercase otherwise
	- its "short direction" is:
		"+" if its direction is up
		"—" otherwise
	- its "short name" is: its short rank + its short suit
	- its "state" is: its short rank + its short suit + its short direction

	## its picture:  a character of unicode's Playing Cards
	// SEE:  https://www.compart.com/en/unicode/block/U+1F0A0
	// The block is a grid:  a row for each suit, and in each row, a column for each rank.
	// - The rows start at 1F0A0 (spades), 1F0B0 (hearts), 1F0C0 (diamonds) and 1F0D0 (clubs).
	// - The columns run ace 1, 2 ... 10, jack B, then a knight our deck doesn't have, C, then queen D and king E.
	- its "picture column" is:
		its value + 1 if it is a queen or it is a king      // past the knight
		its value otherwise
	- its "picture" is:
		unicode 1F0A0 + its picture column if it is a spade
		unicode 1F0B0 + its picture column if it is a heart
		unicode 1F0C0 + its picture column if it is a diamond
		unicode 1F0D0 + its picture column otherwise

	## drawing:  its picture face up, the back every card shares face down
	- to draw it:
		if it is face down
			return <ui-text class="Card" size="massive" color="blue" onClick={fire event card click with card = it}>
				{unicode 1F0A0}
			</ui-text>
		return <ui-text class="Card" size="massive" color={its color} onClick={fire event card click with card = it}>
			{its picture}
		</ui-text>

	## turning it over
	// each pauses a moment, so `wait for: turn the card face up` animates
	- to turn it face up:
		set its direction to up
		pause for 50 msec
	- to turn it face down:
		set its direction to down
		pause for 50 msec
	- to turn it over:
		if it is face up: turn it face down
		otherwise: turn it face up
		pause for 50 msec


## A joker:  a wild card with no rank or suit -- there's a red one and a black one
a "joker" is a card where:
	// set when it's made:  it has no suit to work its color out from
	- its "color" is a color
	- its "name" is: its color + "-joker"           // e.g. "red-joker"
	- its "short name" is "🃏"
	- its "state" is: its short name + its short direction
	- its "picture" is:
		unicode 1F0BF if its color is red
		unicode 1F0CF otherwise


## Tests
to test card setup
	get a new card whose rank is queen, suit is spades and direction is up
	echo it
	its rank should be queen
	its suit should be spades
	its name should be "queen-of-spades"
	its color should be black
	its value should be 12
	its short suit should be "♠️"
	its short rank should be "Q"
	its short name should be "Q♠️"
	its state should be "Q♠️+"
	its picture should be "🂭"

	it is face up should be yes
	it is face down should be no

	it is a face card should be yes
	it is not a face card should be no

	it is a spade should be yes
	it is a club should be no

	it is a queen should be yes
	it is an ace should be no
	it is a 2 should be no

	it is the queen of spades should be yes
	it is the queen of clubs should be no
	it is not the 2 of diamonds should be yes

	turn it face down
	its direction should be down
	it is face down should be yes

	turn it over
	it is face up should be yes

	// a number card:  its rank as it is, and its picture in the row of its suit
	set the seven to a new card whose rank is 7, suit is hearts and direction is up
	the short name of the seven should be "7♥️"
	the color of the seven should be red
	the picture of the seven should be "🂷"
	the picture of a new card whose rank is ace and suit is clubs should be "🃑"
	the picture of a new card whose rank is king and suit is diamonds should be "🃎"

to test jokers
	get a new joker whose color is red and direction is up
	echo it
	it is a joker should be yes
	it is a card should be yes
	its color should be red
	its name should be "red-joker"
	its short name should be "🃏"
	its picture should be "🂿"
	it is the red joker should be yes
	it is the black joker should be no
	it is not the black joker should be yes

	it is face up should be yes
	turn it over
	it is face down should be yes

	set black joker to a new joker whose color is black
	the picture of black joker should be "🃏"

	set the card to a new card whose rank is queen and suit is spades
	the card is a joker should be no
	the card is not a joker should be yes
	the card is the red joker should be no
